Subject: Raise Logto pnpm override floors on the current release line

Origin: DHI-internal (packaged lockfile)
Description: Move existing pnpm override floors to patched versions on the same lines, add floors for @azure/msal-node, source-map-js, and zod 4 at 4.6.6, and raise basic-ftp, nodemailer, postcss-selector-parser, katex, and @simplewebauthn/server to versions that clear catalog CVE findings. pnpm 10.34.8 rewrote pnpm-lock.yaml with --lockfile-only for those floors. qs is then raised from 6.16.0 to 6.16.1 for CVE-2026-110816 by changing only that override and re-running lockfile-only, so the rest of the resolved graph stays put. zod 3.x lockfile copies are unchanged because forcing them to zod 4 breaks @logto/core-kit TypeScript builds. react-router stays on 6.30.6 because 7.18.0 trades medium CVEs for a new high-severity GHSA on the 7.x line and 8.x is not published for react-router-dom.
CVE: CVE-2026-110816
Base-Tree: git https://github.com/logto-io/logto 94c088f9e4f87ba93df1f72ed20edf16ce364f61
Regenerate: on the existing lockfile, change only the qs override, then `CI=true pnpm install --lockfile-only --ignore-scripts` with pnpm 10.34.9
Forwarded: not-needed (floors are applied in the packaged lockfile)
Drop-When: never: the v1.45.0 tag still records the previous override floors

